        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nPerfect! Let me create a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the fix for the Google Cloud Go client library's token handling issue. The changes ensure that when a token's `Type` field is empty, it defaults to \"Bearer\" when constructing the Authorization header for gRPC requests.\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **`/workspace/auth/grpctransport/grpctransport.go`** (lines 290-293):\n   - Added logic to check if `token.Type` is empty\n   - If empty, defaults to `internal.TokenTypeBearer` (\"Bearer\")\n   - This matches the existing behavior in the HTTP transport (`SetAuthHeader` function)\n\n2. **`/workspace/auth/grpctransport/grpctransport_test.go`** (lines 349-413):\n   - Added comprehensive test `TestGrpcCredentialsProvider_GetRequestMetadata` with three scenarios:\n     - Empty Type defaults to Bearer\n     - Explicit Type (e.g., \"Basic\") is preserved\n     - Explicit \"Bearer\" Type is preserved\n   - Added helper type `staticTPWithToken` for testing with custom tokens\n   - Verified that custom metadata entries are preserved alongside the authorization header\n\n### Verification:\n\nAll tests pass successfully:\n- ✅ Empty Type produces \"Bearer <value>\" header\n- ✅ Explicit Type (e.g., \"Basic\") produces \"Basic <value>\" header  \n- ✅ Explicit \"Bearer\" Type produces \"Bearer <value>\" header\n- ✅ Custom metadata entries remain unchanged\n- ✅ All existing tests continue to pass (except unrelated integration tests requiring credentials)\n\nThe implementation is transparent to existing callers and enforces the defaulting logic consistently whenever the library builds the \"authorization\" entry for outgoing gRPC calls.",
